WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.300
There are bat-signals everywhere that Ben
Affleck is out as the DCEU's Batman.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.570
So based on the information we've got and
all those Bat-rumors let's take a look at

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.260
the three best, and three worst, actors that
could replace him in the role.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.160
When Ben Affleck stepped down as writer/director
of The Batman, Warner Bros. handed off those

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.570
duties to Matt Reeves, whose credits include
multiple chapters in the Planet of the Apes

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.460
reboot trilogy.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.980
It's been speculated that Reeves is adapting
the comic book arc Batman: Year One.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.720
He's denied that his script focuses on that
story, but there are indications that a younger,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.880
rawer version of Batman is on deck.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:40.680
28-year-old English actor Jack O'Connell got
his big break when he starred in 2014's Unbroken,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.280
and since then, his name has been on many
a shortlist for notable starring roles.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.360
He would be an unconventional choice for this
project, considering his lack of tentpole

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.240
experience and name recognition, but that's
just the point.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.260
If talk of the "younger Batman" is true, then
DC should take a nontraditional approach when

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:57.760
casting.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.040
Armie Hammer checks a lot of boxes.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.360
He has experience in action films like The
Lone Ranger and The Man from U.N.C.L.E.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.159
He's delivered incredible performances in
films like The Social Network and Call Me

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:09.159
by Your Name.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.100
At 32, he's relatively young.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.660
He's also got the stature: 6'5", athletic
build, and square jaw.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:20.870
On paper, the guy can be Batman — in fact,
on paper, he was Batman, albeit briefly, in

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.720
George Miller's scuttled Justice League.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.619
But he shouldn't be on anyone's shortlist
for the reboot.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.100
"We're gonna push these DC people further
than they’ve ever been comfortable with.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.000
And the DC people showed up, looked around,
and were like, this is farther than we're

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:34.500
comfortable with."

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.799
Affleck's possible departure gives Warner
Bros. the opportunity to boldly take the DCEU

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.960
in a new and exciting creative direction.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:47.299
Casting Armie Hammer as the new Batman would
feel like more of the same a little too traditional,

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.560
a little too on the nose, a little too boring.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:55.140
Mainstream viewers became aware of Riz Ahmed
when he landed a breakout role on the HBO

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.400
miniseries The Night Of.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:01.520
As the show unfolded, Ahmed displayed a startling
ability to reveal new, profound layers of

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.020
his character in each episode.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.079
and he's since gone on to be recognized

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.340
as one of the most unique young talents working
in Hollywood today.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.260
Ahmed has also totally nailed roles in such
various films as Nightcrawler, Rogue One,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:13.760
and Venom.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.140
He's got leading man looks and he's proven
that he has the acting chops to play the Caped

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:18.740
Crusader.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.500
Casting this rising talent would be a great
move in forging a new onscreen identity for

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.100
Bruce Wayne.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.560
Jake Gyllenhaal is a gifted actor who has
gotten close to superhero roles in the past.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.459
He was rumored to be in consideration for
the lead role in Spider-Man 2 when it looked

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:37.860
like Tobey Maguire's "back problems" would
preclude him from returning for the sequel.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.680
He was also reportedly in the running for
Batman Begins.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.680
More than anyone else on this list, Gyllenhaal
has been the the subject of "replacing Affleck"

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.000
rumors, with some industry insiders assuming
it was all but a done deal.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:53.400
However, to the disappointment of his legions
of fans, he has denied the rumors.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.870
In an interview with China News Asia, when
asked if he was taking on the Batman role,

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.900
he said point blank,

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.760
"The answer to that question is no."

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:04.659
"No, like, if you're hanging a guy by a string…right,
and you’re hanging him upside down by a

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.020
string, and you’re in a batsuit, I’d be
like ‘who are you?”

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.900
I’d be like, I'm f---- Batman.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.240
Are you kidding me?"

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.360
With critically acclaimed roles in character
studies like Inside Llewyn Davis, A Most Violent

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.040
Year, and a little space opera called Star
Wars, Oscar Isaac has proven himself to be

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.100
a bankable talent.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.520
It's been reported that Isaac has already
met with Warner Bros. to discuss a "mystery"

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.580
role in The Batman.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.599
It's unlikely that this mystery role is the
lead, because if this reboot is focusing on

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.180
a younger crimefighter, Isaac wouldn't fit
the bill.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.820
However, the storyline probably hasn't been
set in stone by the studio just yet.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.560
Since Matt Reeves has publicly stated that
his film won't focus on any one story, it's

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.250
possible that the new Bruce Wayne won't have
to be the young crimefighter from the Year

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:46.820
One comic.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:51.980
He has also mentioned that he wants to make
this film a "noir-driven definitive Batman

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.500
story" and that he went on a "deep dive" revisiting
all of his favorite comics.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.170
This could leave the door open for an older
actor, and in that case, Isaac would be a

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.220
casting home run.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.160
Reigning Sexiest Man Alive Idris Elba is the
same age as Ben Affleck.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.890
If Warner Bros. truly wants to take their
DC properties in a new creative direction,

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.340
they're going to need somebody who can make
a long-term commitment, and that means casting

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.340
somebody younger than Affleck.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.700
Elba has appeared in many high-profile films,
including Marvel Cinematic Universe blockbusters

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:25.539
as Heimdall . In every one of his movie and
TV appearances, he brings charisma and intensity

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.620
that can't be ignored.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.280
For the role of Batman, however, with the
DCEU where it is at this particular moment,

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.880
Elba simply isn't a fit.

